 "sections": [
  {
   "heading": "(页面开头)",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "kind": "p",
     "text": "Ship movement in Nebulous Fleet Command is similar to that of submarines or oceangoing ships, with max speeds and drag."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "heading": "Mechanics",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 1,
     "text": "Thrust: speed limit as a fraction of max speed. Options are 1/3 (33%), 2/3 (66%), Full (100%), Flank (150%), and Flight Quarters (FQ, 100%, with carrier green-deck handling). Acceleration uses full thrust at every setting; only Flank adds 50% forward thrust."
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 1,
     "text": "Acceleration: This mostly is affected by the drives, however the mass of the ship based on installed components slightly affects acceleration."
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 1,
     "text": "Flank Speed: Boosts top speed by 50% (does not affect turn speed or turn acceleration). When flanking, every active thruster checks for flank damage once per second, and takes 5 damage if the check fails. Forward acceleration is additionally increased by 50%"
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 1,
     "text": "Heading/Roll: Holds the ship pointing in a certain direction or oriented \"up\" a certain way"
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 1,
     "text": "Drives as main modifier"
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 1,
     "text": "Dodging & Evasive: EVADE posture applies a slight \"corkscrew\" to travel. This allows small ships to sometimes dodge shots. Skilled players may issue move orders or the orbit command to dodge shots, which is far more effective than the EVADE setting."
    },
    {
     "kind": "p",
     "text": "When a target is lost and there are no remaining roll drivers, the ship will issue itself a temporary ROL order to prevent re-masking weapons."
    },
