      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 1,
     "text": "[math]\\displaystyle{ P \\equiv \\text{Angular Thrust (as seen in-game)} }[/math]"
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 1,
     "text": "[math]\\displaystyle{ M \\equiv \\text{Ship Mass (as seen in-game)} }[/math]"
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 1,
     "text": "[math]\\displaystyle{ F \\equiv \\text{Ship Inertia Factor (see chart)} }[/math]"
    },
    {
     "kind": "p",
     "text": "Because of damping, ships will accelerate only to a certain maximum speed given by (in radians per second), [math]\\displaystyle{ \\omega_\\text{max} = \\frac{1000P}{MF} }[/math]"
    },
    {
     "kind": "p",
     "text": "The time in seconds, [math]\\displaystyle{ t }[/math], to turn 180° is: [math]\\displaystyle{ \\large{{t \\approx \\frac{\\pi}{\\omega_\\text{max}} + 10}} }[/math]"
    },
    {
     "kind": "p",
     "text": "([math]\\displaystyle{ \\omega_\\text{max} }[/math] is usually smaller than the listed max turn rate, [math]\\displaystyle{ R }[/math], except for buffed light ships and possibly when rolling. To compare the two, take [math]\\displaystyle{ R }[/math], multiply by [math]\\displaystyle{ \\pi }[/math], and divide by 180. If the result is [math]\\displaystyle{ < \\omega_\\text{max} }[/math], then replace [math]\\displaystyle{ \\omega_\\text{max} }[/math] in the equation above by the result.)"
    }
   ]
