  {
   "heading": "Formation",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "kind": "p",
     "text": "Formations allow for ships to be grouped together and commanded as one unit. Ships in a formation will attempt to maintain a certain position relative to the guide/lead ship, and will match speed and heading with the lead ship. If the formation becomes too separated while manoeuvring, ships will slow down to allow other ships to catch up."
    },
    {
     "kind": "p",
     "text": "Formations have 3 modes:"
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 1,
     "text": "Rel: Maintains relative positions around the lead ship according to its heading, allowing the formation to rotate with the lead ship."
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 1,
     "text": "Tru: Maintains a fixed position around the lead ship, and does not adjust the formation if the lead rotates. Ships will still rotate to match the lead's heading"
    },
    {
     "kind": "li",
     "depth": 1,
     "text": "Loose: Similar to Tru, but the formation will not slow down for the slower ships and will be allowed to outrun each-other."
    },
    {
     "kind": "p",
     "text": "Holding shift and giving orders issues the order to the entire formation. This includes changing settings on the status panel. If you select a ship in the formation that is not the lead ship, and give it a movement order, the ship will exit the formation to complete its order."
    }
   ]
